---
import katex from 'katex';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chain from '../components/Chain.astro';
import StatusTable from '../components/StatusTable.astro';
const chiR = katex.renderToString('\\chi_R', { throwOnError: false });
---
<Base legend={true}>
  <header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="kicker">Quantized Information Quantum Theory — Holographic</div>
    <h1>One wave function, one world.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The global wave function Φ evolves exactly unitarily — no collapse term, ever.
      Decoherence makes the macroscopic records non-interfering; a non-dynamical selector <em>λ</em> makes
      exactly one of them <em>actual</em>. One wave function, one world. The holographic capacity bound
      gives the finite record <em>stage</em> (how many distinguishable records a region can hold) — it does
      <em>not</em> force the single outcome: the honest crux is that the single record is λ's doing (an
      Everett-like selection), not capacity's, and that selection is a postulate, not yet derived.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/idea">Read the idea</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/theory">The mathematics</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/papers">Papers &amp; arXiv</a>
    </div>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--st-conditional)"></span>
        <b>A research program</b>, not a finished theory — conditional, Born reduced but still open</span>
      <span class="chip"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--st-verified)"></span>
        <b>Machine-verified</b> in Lean&nbsp;4 / Mathlib · no <code>sorry</code> · reproducible</span>
    </div>
  </div></header>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>The argument in five links</h2>
    <p class="sub">The whole thesis is one chain. Two links are postulates (the finite stage and the
      λ-selection), two are machine-verified / standard physics, and one is open (Born, reduced). Each is
      labelled honestly — including that holography is the stage, not the mechanism.</p>
    <Chain />
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>What is proven, what is open</h2>
    <p class="sub">Honesty is the point. The axiom-free Lean development verifies the modular /
      relative-entropy calculus (<span set:html={chiR} />), the covariant consistent Born measure, and the
      Born-from-typicality reduction — not the (FQ) holographic axiom, not λ's dynamical law, not the
      continuum. (The original "capacity forbids records" conjecture is retired, not pending.)</p>
    <StatusTable />
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Explore</h2>
    <div class="cards" style="margin-top:18px">
      <a class="card" href="/idea"><h3>The Idea</h3>
        <p>The measurement problem, finite information, and single outcomes, in plain language.</p>
        <span class="arrow">Start here →</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/theory"><h3>The Theory</h3>
        <p>The (FQ) axiom, <span set:html={chiR} />, Type&nbsp;II algebras, the retired H2 conjecture, and single outcomes by λ.</p>
        <span class="arrow">Read the math →</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/selection"><h3>Φ &amp; λ</h3>
        <p>Constitution and actuality: the global wave function, and which admissible record is real.</p>
        <span class="arrow">The picture →</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/formalization"><h3>Formalization</h3>
        <p>The Lean&nbsp;4 / Mathlib machine-checked substrate, theorem index, reproducible build.</p>
        <span class="arrow">See the proofs →</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/open-problems"><h3>Open Problems</h3>
        <p>The four gaps between a research program and a theory, and what closing each buys.</p>
        <span class="arrow">The frontier →</span></a>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</Base>
